{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Morning. Do come in and have a seat. I'm Dr Shah. What's brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Cough.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): A cough. How would you describe it?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Dry.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long has it been going on?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Three weeks.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): What do you think set it off?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Cold.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Did you have a blocked nose and a runny nose with that cold?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Has the blocked nose and runny nose cleared now?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Cleared.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any phlegm with the cough?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any blood when you cough?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Are you short of breath walking about?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): How have you been sleeping with all this?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Ramipril.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): We'll get to the ramipril, promise. Does the cough wake you at night?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any wheeze?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any chest tightness?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Have you felt feverish at all?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): You're on treatment for high blood pressure. Which tablet are you on now?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Ramipril.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ramipril five milligrams, once a day, for the blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): When did you start it?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Month.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): About a month ago. Do you know the exact date?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Dunno.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): And before the ramipril, were you on a different tablet for the blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Amlodipine.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Are you still taking the amlodipine?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Stopped in March.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): What made you stop?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Swelling.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ankle swelling, and it's settled since?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): So, amlodipine five milligrams for the blood pressure, stopped in March. Have I got that right?",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): Were you ever given enalapril?",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is there anyone in the family on a blood pressure tablet?",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (PATIENT): Sister.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): What does she take?",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): Lisinopril.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (DOCTOR): That's her tablet, not one you take?",
  "[SEG0054] person_2 (PATIENT): Hers.",
  "[SEG0055] person_1 (DOCTOR): The car park was a right state this morning, wasn't it?",
  "[SEG0056] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0057] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0058] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0059] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll check your blood pressure. It's 146 over 88, and your pulse is 74. Chest is clear both sides, no wheeze, and your throat looks fine.",
  "[SEG0060] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0061] person_1 (DOCTOR): Um, thinking it through, this dry cough could be the ramipril. ACE inhibitors like ramipril and enalapril, and your sister's lisinopril, sometimes give a tickly cough, but it might just be the tail of that cold. I'm not making a firm diagnosis today.",
  "[SEG0062] person_2 (PATIENT): Cold.",
  "[SEG0063] person_1 (DOCTOR): You still put it down to the cold, which is fair, we really can't be sure. I'll stop the ramipril and switch you to, um, candesartan— well, actually, losartan, fifty milligrams once a day by mouth, for the blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0064] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0065] person_1 (DOCTOR): Stop the ramipril from today and start the losartan. If the cough hasn't settled in four weeks we might arrange a chest x-ray, but I won't book one now. I'll see you back in four weeks to recheck your blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0066] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine."
 ],
